      "text": "FIRST DEBATE (1930s-1940s):\n  IDEALISM vs. REALISM\n  Idealism (Norman Angell, Woodrow Wilson):\n  War is irrational; international law, collective\n  security, and liberal institutions can eliminate it.\n  WWII answered this debate for a generation.\n  Realism (E.H. Carr *The Twenty Years' Crisis*, 1939;\n  Morgenthau *Politics Among Nations*, 1948): power,\n  not law, governs international relations."
